From b3622b092d9d022e1ea740ef558b548b5a2f1c4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:17:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: say at what depth and in what format HDR
 leaves

The question of the HDR10 depth guard (DVBRIDGE_HDR10_DEEP_COLOR, a
TEST_ONLY commit) told only whether Dolby Vision rebuilt as HDR10 left
at 10 bits or more or at 8, and only for that. With linux-9966..9969
the kernel answers it in DVBRIDGE_LINK_FORMAT, a read-only bitmask
written from the check of every request of the guard: one bit for the
format of the configuration (rgb, ycbcr444, ycbcr422, ycbcr420) and one
for its bits per component (6bpc to 16bpc), with any HDR metadata or
none.

Kodi now asks it for every HDR output, HDR10 and HLG as well as Dolby
Vision rebuilt as HDR10 (ProbeOutputDepth(), which replaces
ProbeDVConversionDepth()): once the HDR signalling has gone out, again
after a change of mode, with another video and when the signalling
changes; not during native Dolby Vision. It reads the answer with
DVBRIDGE::LINK::Parse() (one format and one depth, or nothing), which a
host test runs on every value the kernel can give. The answer goes:
- to kodi.log: "HDR output: HDR10 goes out as YCbCr 4:2:0 at 10 bits in
  3840x2160 @ 59.940 Hz", and at 8 bits why: "8-bit RGB" chosen in the
  settings, or the link carries no more;
- to the overview page of the player information: the bits per
  component and the format, "as the driver says" (before, only the most
  that max bpc lets through, which is still what SDR and NVIDIA show);
- to the Dolby Vision page, for a picture rebuilt as HDR10: "HDR10, 10
  bits, YCbCr 4:2:0".
Where the driver has the guard without DVBRIDGE_LINK_FORMAT, HDR10 is
told at 10 bits or more, or at 8, as before; HLG then is not told.
Nothing is changed for the question: the picture goes out as it would
without it.

New Estuary strings 31984-31986 (es_es, es_ar, es_mx).
